# Defect Workflow Guardrails

When changing defect generation, sync, regression, or column behavior, update **all**
layers listed in `.cursor/rules/defect-pipeline-doc-sync.mdc` in the same change.

## Single Status column (hard)

Defect rows (local Excel + Google **Defects** tab) use **one** column: **Status**.

- **Allowed values:** `New`, `In Progress`, `Resolved`, `Reopened`, `Closed`
- **Forbidden columns:** `Dev Status`, `QA Status`, and legacy split-status schemas
- **Default on raise:** `New` when QA or pipeline first registers a failure
- **Dropdown:** apply on local Excel column M and Google `Defects!M2:M500`

Schema: `specs/generated/qa-pipeline/schemas/defect-workbook-schema.json`

## Severity & Priority (set at defect generation only)

**Milestone routing (hard):** Defect workbooks and Google rows go under
`pipeline/test-data/Milestone{N}/Defects/` where **N** is resolved from Stage 0
artifacts — Test Cases + FSD + Figma under `pipeline/test-data/Milestone{N}/`.
Each failed **Test Case ID** maps to the milestone whose Excel workbook contains
that ID (`resolve-defect-milestone.cjs`). Spec path alone does not override the
workbook mapping when the TC ID is found in Milestone Excel.

| Milestone folder has Test Cases + FSD + Figma | Defect output |
|-----------------------------------------------|---------------|
| Milestone1 only (for that module's TC IDs) | `Milestone1/Defects/` |
| Milestone2 only (for that module's TC IDs) | `Milestone2/Defects/` |

**Severity** and **Priority** are assigned **once** inside `generateDefectFiles` when
defect rows are created from the **test execution report** (immediately after
Playwright finishes — not on a separate post-defect step).

| Field | When set | How |
|-------|----------|-----|
| **Severity** | Test run → `failureRecords` → `createWorkbook` | Product impact from failure evidence (Critical / High / Medium / Low). Classifier: `pipeline/scripts/classify-defect-severity-priority.cjs` |
| **Priority** | Same moment | Fix urgency: test-case Excel **Priority** adjusted by execution impact. **Independent** from Severity — never copied from it |

| Actor | May change Severity/Priority? |
|-------|------------------------------|
| `generateDefectFiles` (after test run) | **Yes** — for failed cases in that run |
| Google sync upsert | **Fill only when sheet cell is empty**; preserve existing values |
| defect-regression | **Never** |
| Post-generation backfill / metadata-only sync | **Never** (no backfill script) |

Re-run: a **new test execution** that fails again regenerates the **local** defect row
with fresh Severity/Priority for that failure. Google preserves values once written.

## Who may change Status

| Actor | May change Status? | Rules |
|-------|-------------------|--------|
| QA pipeline / execute-raise-defects | On **new** rows only | Set `New` when creating; preserve existing Status on upsert |
| Humans (Excel / Google) | Yes | Dev/QA manual workflow |
| **defect-regression** agent | **Only Resolved → Closed/Reopened on Google** | After anchor TC re-test; **Google Defects tab only** |

## Defect regression — hard boundaries

Invoke `@.cursor/agents/defect-regression.agent.md` / `defect-regression` for retest
work — do not run regression status logic in the parent session.

| Current Status | Enter regression? | Automated status change? |
|----------------|-------------------|---------------------------|
| **New** | No | **Never** |
| **In Progress** | No | **Never** |
| **Resolved** | Yes | Yes → **Closed** (pass) or **Reopened** (fail) |
| **Reopened** | No | **Never** (until human sets back to Resolved) |
| **Closed** | No | **Never** |

Defect regression **touches Resolved only** — never New, In Progress, Reopened, or Closed.

Mechanical enforcement:

- `read-defect-sheet.cjs` / `loadRegressionDefects` — reads **Google Defects tab only**; filters `Status = Resolved`
- `defect-regression-run.js` — rejects `--source local` / `--workbook`; requires CDP Chrome
- `deriveStatusUpdates()` — skips non-Resolved defects
- `update-defect-google-statuses.cjs` — writes Status **on Google only**; skips rows whose current Status is not Resolved; logs `skipped[]`
- Local defect Excel is **not** read or updated by defect-regression

Command: `npm run tracker:cdp-chrome` then `npm run qa:defect-regression -- --milestone <N>`  
Google Status is written **automatically** after regression (no **Approve defects**). Opt out: `--defer-google-sync`.

## Upsert / sync preservation

When upserting defects from pipeline or execute-raise-defects:

- **Preserve** existing `Status` when the row already exists (local + Google)
- **Never** reset `In Progress`, `Resolved`, `Closed`, or `Reopened` back to `New` from stale local Excel
- **Preserve** existing **Severity** and **Priority** on Google when already set; fill only when empty
- **`--metadata-only`** sync skips Status, Severity, and Priority entirely
- Only **defect-regression** may write `Closed` / `Reopened`, and only from **Resolved**

## Must not

- Emit or require Dev Status + QA Status in new defect workbooks
- Change Status on **New**, **In Progress**, **Reopened**, or **Closed** during regression
- Update Severity/Priority after defect generation (backfill, regression, or metadata-only sync)
- Mirror Priority into Severity or vice versa
- `append-defects-google-sheet.js` — `mergeRegressionStatus()` blocks Closed/Reopened writes unless existing Status is Resolved
- Mark regression **Done** without mechanical `skipped` / `applied` evidence when updates were attempted
- Bypass `defect-regression` agent for Resolved retest → Closed/Reopened workflow
- Change defect pipeline behavior in scripts only without updating agents, rules, schemas, `AGENTS.md`, and `project-context.mdc`
